in D.C. these days?

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:02.956 align:start size:84% position:16%
- (sighs) Yeah, yeah,
it kind of does.

00:02:02.956 --> 00:02:04.591
Let's unpack that a lot.

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:07.427
One, I think it's political
malfeasance on their part.

00:02:07.427 --> 00:02:11.030 align:start size:97% position:3%
I see a lot more Republicans
go on left wing shows.

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:13.299
I like doing it,
I've done it a lot.

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:16.002
And frankly, it's
good for your...

00:02:16.002 --> 00:02:19.105 align:start size:94% position:6%
If you only care about
catering to your own base,

00:02:19.105 --> 00:02:20.640 align:start size:84% position:16%
it's actually
still good for that

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:23.276
because you base still loves
watching you say, you know,

00:02:23.276 --> 00:02:24.944 align:start size:97% position:3%
go toe-to-toe with somebody
who disagrees with you.

00:02:24.944 --> 00:02:25.912 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Especially if you get them.
- Right, right.

00:02:25.912 --> 00:02:27.313
- That's what they really like.

00:02:27.313 --> 00:02:29.115 align:start size:97% position:3%
- And it's fun, it's
intellectually stimulating.

00:02:29.115 --> 00:02:31.317
There's a lot of other
reasons I like doing it.

00:02:31.317 --> 00:02:33.453
But most, I mean,
most importantly,

00:02:33.453 --> 00:02:35.054
you know I always
say like politics,

00:02:35.054 --> 00:02:38.424
fighting in politics, what
is fighting in politics?

00:02:38.424 --> 00:02:40.693 align:start size:88% position:13%
Fighting in politics
means persuading others.

00:02:40.693 --> 00:02:43.263
That's the metric
by which you fight.

00:02:43.263 --> 00:02:44.731 align:start size:84% position:16%
A lot of people think
otherwise, right?

00:02:44.731 --> 00:02:46.299
It's just yelling and
screaming and picketing

00:02:46.299 --> 00:02:49.802 align:start size:97% position:3%
and doing all that and maybe,
you know, dying on hills

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:51.004
that you knew you
were gonna die on.

00:02:51.004 --> 00:02:52.272
That's not fighting.

00:02:52.272 --> 00:02:53.673 align:start size:84% position:16%
That's fighting for
your base's attention.

00:02:53.673 --> 00:02:54.974
That's a certain kind of fight.

00:02:54.974 --> 00:02:56.276
But you're not really
fighting for them.

00:02:56.276 --> 00:02:57.844
And so fighting
means persuading.

00:02:57.844 --> 00:02:59.512
And the best way to persuade
is to get your point across

00:02:59.512 --> 00:03:01.514
in a reasonable manner on a show

00:03:01.514 --> 00:03:05.818
where you know the audience
generally disagrees with you.

00:03:05.818 --> 00:03:06.986
So, yeah, I don't get it.

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:08.154 align:start size:84% position:16%
So I think it's
political malfeasance.

00:03:08.154 --> 00:03:10.323
